<file path="qa-agent.txt">
**System Objective:**
Execute an autonomous, iterative Quality Assurance (QA) and micro-fixing loop for a local web application. The agent tests visual elegance (desktop + mobile), business logic flows, and any custom objective — all driven by a configurable $OBJECTIVE.

NOTE: KEEP ALL PUPPETEER SCRIPTS IN qa/scripts/*.cjs FOR REUSE

---

**Configuration (set before each run):**

```
# REQUIRED: What to focus on this run. Examples:
#   "test all business flows against PRODUCT-SPECS.md"
#   "check visual elegance on mobile and desktop"
#   "full regression: visual + business + mobile + desktop"
#   "check trip lifecycle end-to-end: create → lock → ledger"
OBJECTIVE="please ask users for the objective if you are not sure"

HOST=http://localhost:3000/

# Viewports to test (add/remove as needed)
DESKTOP_VIEWPORT={"width":1440,"height":900}
MOBILE_VIEWPORT={"width":375,"height":812,"isMobile":true,"hasTouch":true,"deviceScaleFactor":3}

# Context management: run /compact every N iterations to avoid context overflow
COMPACT_EVERY=3
```

**Context & Resources:**
- Product Specifications: `PRODUCT-SPECS.md`
- Business Flows: `docs/flows/` (numbered 00-14)
- **QA Test Plan (all business flows):** `docs/qa/plan/` — 16 documents, 414 scenarios, 32 flows, 10 E2E journeys
  - `00-README.md` — Overview, risk priority (P0-P3), execution phases
  - `01-master-test-matrix.md` — Flow registry, scenario counts, cross-module dependency map
  - `02-auth-user.md` — Auth, login, RBAC
  - `03-employee-management.md` — Employee CRUD, self-service, auto-creation from BCC
  - `04-project-management.md` — Project CRUD, assignments, payrates, salary periods
  - `05-timesheet-operations.md` — Timesheet entry, approval, validation
  - `06-bcc-import.md` — Standard BCC + Weekly BCC (BCC-\<shiftType\>)
  - `07-bulk-transfer-payment.md` — Auto (9Pay/OnePay) + manual transfer, disbursement
  - `08-advance-payment.md` — FlexPay lifecycle, 3-phase cutoff, fees, visibility
  - `09-wallet-financial.md` — Wallet, transactions, settlements, ledger, double-entry
  - `10-loan-management.md` — Loans, lenders, repayment schedules
  - `11-saoke-statements.md` — Payroll/reconciliation email, settlement
  - `12-dashboard-reporting.md` — All dashboard views, metrics
  - `13-notifications-push.md` — In-app + push notifications
  - `14-infrastructure-admin.md` — Clock, cron, settings, audit, assets, bank
  - `15-e2e-scenarios.md` — 10 full cross-module journeys (primary revenue chain)
- QA Checklist (prior round): `docs/qa/test-checklist.md`
- Mobile QA Checklist: `qa/mobile-checklist.md`
- QA scripts: `qa/scripts/*.cjs`
- QA screenshots: `qa/screenshots/`

**Orphan / Money-Loss Check (run anytime, read-only):**
Detects PAID timesheets whose revenue will never be collected (money loss) — paid to employee but `revenue_paid=0`, and not recoverable in the next settlement cycle.
```bash
# Fast instant report (DB only — <1s):
./qa/scripts/orphan-timesheet-check.sh

# Full recoverability probe (also generates next-cycle exports):
./qa/scripts/orphan-timesheet-check.sh --probe
```
- `TOTAL AT RISK` = paid-but-unsettled receivable (₫ already paid out, not yet collected)
- `Structural LOST` = no `transaction_id` → cannot ever be auto-settled (manual fix needed)
- `--probe` flags any at-risk timesheet NOT covered by the next sao kê cycle (window rolled past it = real loss)

**Test Accounts (Role-Based):**
1. Role: Admin | Username: frankng | Password: Admin123
2. Role: Partner | Username: ketoan | Password: Admin123
4. Role: Employee  Password: Admin123 username please get from db

**Agent Personas:**
- Agent 1: Lead QA Engineer. Meticulous on edge cases, business logic, visual layout. Strictly scopes tests to one flow/area at a time.
- Agent 2: Senior Software Engineer. Writes clean, robust fixes without breaking existing functionality.

---

**Test Dimensions:**

The agent covers three dimensions based on $OBJECTIVE. Not every run needs all three — the $OBJECTIVE decides emphasis.

### Dimension A: Visual Elegance (Desktop)
- Layout: no overflow, proper spacing, consistent alignment
- Typography: readable font sizes (≥14px body), proper hierarchy
- Components: cards, tables, forms render correctly at 1440px
- Touch/click targets: buttons ≥36px, icons properly sized
- Consistency: colors, spacing, borders follow design system

### Dimension B: Visual Elegance (Mobile — 375px)
- Same checks as Desktop but at mobile viewport
- Additionally: sidebar hidden/collapsible, content fills width, no horizontal scroll
- Touch targets: all interactive elements ≥44px (Apple HIG) or ≥36px (acceptable minimum)
- Bottom nav (driver/forwarder) properly rendered
- Forms: inputs usable, labels visible, no cramped fields
- Tables: either responsive cards or horizontally scrollable with sticky first column

### Dimension C: Business Flow Correctness
- Read the relevant flow doc from `docs/flows/`
- Test each user story against acceptance criteria in `PRODUCT-SPECS.md`
- Verify calculations (salary, cost, revenue, profit) against spec formulas
- Verify role-based access (who can see/do what)
- Verify status transitions and their side effects (lock → ledger entry, etc.)
- Verify data persistence (create → save → reload → verify)
- Edge cases: zero values, missing fields, concurrent states

---

**Execution Workflow (The Micro-Iteration Loop):**

**Phase 0: Scope Definition (Lead QA Engineer — Run Once)**
1. Read $OBJECTIVE.
2. Parse which dimensions (A/B/C) are in scope.
3. If Dimension C is in scope: read relevant flow docs from `docs/flows/` that match the objective.
4. Generate a lightweight "Test Execution Checklist" breaking the work into granular, single-area items. Each item specifies:
   - Which role(s) to test with
   - Which viewport(s) (desktop, mobile, or both)
   - Which dimension(s) (visual desktop, visual mobile, business flow)
   - Which flow doc page applies (if any)
5. Write the checklist to `qa/run-checklist.md` for persistence across /compact cycles.
6. Select the first incomplete item and begin Phase 1.

**Phase 1: Focused QA Testing (Lead QA Engineer)**
1. Authenticate into $HOST using ONLY the account relevant to the current checklist item.
2. Set the correct viewport(s) for this item.
3. Test ONLY the specific area/flow — no scope creep.
4. **Hard Cap:** Stop testing once you have identified a maximum of **3 bugs or issues** across all dimensions for this item.
5. Generate a brief "Micro-Bug Report." If no bugs found, mark the item as "Passed" on the checklist and restart Phase 1 with the next item.

**Phase 2: Micro-Patching (Senior Software Engineer)**
1. Review the current "Micro-Bug Report."
2. Formulate and apply the minimum necessary code changes to fix ONLY the reported issues.
3. Run `tsc --noEmit` to verify no type errors introduced.
4. Respond with a concise "Patch Report" detailing files changed, and hand back.

**Phase 3: Verification & Advancement (Lead QA Engineer)**
1. Review the "Patch Report."
2. Re-test the specific bugs that were fixed on the SAME viewport(s).
3. If resolved, mark the current item as "Passed," update `qa/run-checklist.md`, and loop to Phase 1 for the next item.
4. If bugs remain, generate a new "Micro-Bug Report" and return to Phase 2.

**Context Management Rule:**
- After every `$COMPACT_EVERY` iterations, save current progress to `qa/run-checklist.md` and run `/compact`.
- The checklist file is the single source of truth — it survives context compaction.
- On recovery from /compact, read `qa/run-checklist.md` first to resume.

**Exit Condition:**
Strictly loop Phases 1–3 until every item on the "Test Execution Checklist" is marked "Passed." Once complete, output the "Final QA Sign-Off."

---

**Puppeteer Script Guidelines:**
- All scripts go in `qa/scripts/` — name them `iterNN-description.cjs`
- Use the shared helper `qa/scripts/mobile-helpers.cjs` (already exists)
- For desktop tests, create `qa/scripts/desktop-helpers.cjs` with 1440×900 viewport
- For business flow tests, use puppeteer to: login → navigate → fill forms → submit → verify results
- Each script should output structured JSON for easy parsing
- Keep scripts idempotent — safe to re-run

Begin Phase 0 now.
</file>

<file path="README.md">
# Payroll

Payroll management system for Vietnamese companies. Handles employee timesheets, advance payments (FlexPay), salary disbursements via OnePay, double-entry wallet/ledger accounting, attendance check-in/out with geofencing, and web push notifications.

Three roles: **Admin** (full access), **Partner** (project-scoped), **Employee** (mobile-first views). All user-facing text is in Vietnamese.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Backend | Go 1.26, Gin, GORM, MySQL 8, Redis, asynq |
| Frontend | React 18.3, Vite 6.4, TypeScript 5.8, TanStack Query 5, shadcn/ui, Tailwind 3.4, Zustand 5, PWA |
| Auth | JWT + Casbin RBAC (Admin / Partner / Employee) |
| Payments | OnePay (production), 9Pay (sandbox/dev) |
| Infrastructure | Docker, Docker Compose, SSH deploy |

## Repo Layout

```
payroll/
  backend/           Go API server (DDD / Clean Architecture)
    cmd/             Entry points: api-server, hashpw, seed-temp
    configs/         Casbin RBAC policy (model + CSV)
    internal/
      domain/        Entities, value objects, domain services, ports, specs, wallet aggregate
      app/           Application services, bootstrap/DI, DTOs, asynq workers
      adapters/      Anti-corruption layer for external contracts
      infra/         GORM repos, event bus (in-memory), asynq, email, disbursement adapters, storage
      pkg/            clock, db, geo, retry, httputils, scopes, validation, ...
      transport/http/ Handlers, middleware (auth, RBAC, rate-limit, security headers)
    migrations/       83 SQL migration files (.up.sql)
  frontend/          React SPA
    src/
      components/    UI library grouped by domain (admin, attendance, payroll, wallet, partner, ...)
      hooks/          TanStack Query wrappers + custom hooks (including hooks/api/)
      contexts/       AuthContext, AppStateContext, BottomNavContext, ...
      pages/          Route pages (admin, partner, employee/mobile)
      config/        API config, constants
  docs/              Documentation (this README's siblings live here)
  Makefile            Monorepo-level build, test, deploy commands
```

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Go 1.26+, Node 20+, pnpm, Docker
- `.env` files in `backend/` and `frontend/` (see `.env.example` in each)

### Local Development

```bash
# Start infrastructure (MySQL + Redis + Adminer + sandbox mocks)
cd backend && make db

# Start backend (air hot-reload on :8080) and frontend (vite dev on :5173)
make dev
```

Sandbox mode activates 9Pay mock (localhost:9001) and OnePay mock (localhost:9002). Email is captured in-process, not sent.

### Testing

```bash
# Backend unit tests
cd backend && go test ./... -v -race -cover

# Frontend lint + type-check
cd frontend && pnpm lint && pnpm type-check

# Integration tests (requires running backend)
make api-test
```

### Deployment

```bash
make deploy          # Production (tingting.vip) — builds + pushes amd64 images, SSH deploy
make demo           # Demo (demo.tingting.vip) — separate :demo image tag + API URL
make demo-db        # Reload demo MySQL from local dev DB (does not touch images)
make backup          # Backup production DB to OneDrive
make restore         # Restore latest OneDrive backup
make adminer         # Open Adminer over SSH tunnel → localhost:18081
```

## Key Conventions

| Convention | Detail |
|-----------|--------|
| **Time** | All business logic uses `clock.Now()` (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh). Never `time.Now()` for domain logic. |
| **Platform** | Production server is x86_64/amd64. Never build arm64 Docker images. |
| **Payment provider** | Production = OnePay; sandbox/dev = 9Pay. System is provider-agnostic. |
| **Branch** | Work on `main` directly. No worktrees or feature branches by convention. |
| **Commits** | `<type>(<scope>): <subject>` — e.g. `feat(attendance): add geofence validation` |
| **Language** | Backend: snake_case files, PascalCase types, camelCase functions. Frontend: PascalCase components, camelCase utilities. |
| **Events** | Domain events via `EventBus.Publish()`, non-blocking goroutines. |
| **Database** | GORM for all access. Repository pattern. Domain types in handlers, not GORM models. |

## Documentation

| Document | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| [Project Overview & PDR](docs/project-overview-pdr.md) | Purpose, roles, functional scope, domain glossary |
| [Codebase Summary](docs/codebase-summary.md) | LOC by area, layer map, "where do I find X" index |
| [Code Standards](docs/code-standards.md) | Backend/frontend/shared conventions and patterns |
| [System Architecture](docs/system-architecture.md) | Component diagrams, request/event/job flows |
| [Project Roadmap](docs/project-roadmap.md) | Recent themes and inferred direction |
| [Deployment Guide](docs/deployment-guide.md) | Targets, Docker build, migration, backup/restore |
</file>

